	(text_box "Dielectric Absorption (Ceramic Capacitor Distortions)\n- For any capacitor actually touching the audio signal, use Film capacitors (Polypropylene is king) or C0G/NP0 ceramics. These are stable and won't \"color\" or crackle the sound.\n\nResistors (Choosing the Right Material (The \"Crackle\" Factor)\n- Thin Film / Metal Film (Recommended): These are the gold standard for audio. They have very low noise and high stability. If you are using surface-mount parts, look for \"Thin Film\" resistors.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 38.735 169.545 0)
		(size 67.31 19.685)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type dash)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "674ab3f3-75db-4baf-8c01-95efeed74e1e")
	)
	(text "ICS-40730:\nOutput Impedance:\n- OUTPUT+ is 180 Ohms\n- OUTPUT- is 250 Ohms\n- Differential is 430 Ohms\nFrequency Response: \n- From 20 Hz to 20 kHz\nMaximum Output Voltage:\n- Single-Ended, 123 dB SPL input is 0.40V rms\n  This is Vpp≈1.13 V.\nOutput DC Offset: \n- OUTPUT+ is 0.72V\n- OUTPUT- is 0.66V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 33.528 83.82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "03dffdd9-e840-43a9-9f63-7c610f07e400")
	)
	(text "length-matched"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 242.316 74.422 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
		)
		(uuid "0c6f3920-f658-4402-b78d-d2ae30bea3a3")
	)
	(text "Rg"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 110.49 71.374 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
		)
		(uuid "2cd23a6e-ed54-4e4a-8ced-359dce61ccdc")
	)
	(text "The two resistors set the\nopen loop gain\nG = 2.5 Per leg\nRFB = 500 Ohm\nRG = 200 Ohm"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 73.406 43.434 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "2edf10fe-9854-4388-8ed0-462e22ec2141")
	)
	(text "Amplify Microphone output: 0.4Vrms (0.565685424949Vpeak)\n0.565685424949Vpeak*2 = 1.1313708499Vpp\nto 2.82Vpp with 2.5V DC\n2.82V/1.1313708499Vpp = 2.49255140368 Gain"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 182.118 137.668 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "31a376c6-c154-47fb-8fc3-fd832ad985b2")
	)
	(text "R analog sound: \nThin Film/Metal Film (Recommended)\nRg variable"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 103.632 55.118 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "34c93822-5e9f-4162-b285-178cf8ba39ff")
	)
	(text "- DISABLE is asserted by applying a low\n- The DISABLE pin features an internal pull-up network that \n  enables the amplifier for normal operation. The ADA4940-1/ ADA4940-2 \n  DISABLE pin can be left floating (that is, no external connection is \n  required) and does not require an external pull-up resistor to ensure \n  normal on operation"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 168.148 119.38 0)
